## US-138026: New HM Import One time – Prior Data Dump

**Q1. Which file format will the mainframe send, and will it include a record count?** *(PO + Mainframe team)*
- **Story reference:** Scope "Text File pipe delimited, Layout – see attached" and "reconciliation of imported records"; AC1; Synopsis "same file layout … as the CHM import".
- **Question:** The story says the file is pipe-delimited, but the attached layout gives fixed character positions (250 characters per line, no delimiters). Which format will actually be sent? Will the file also carry a total record count so we can confirm every record arrived?
- **Why we ask:** The file reader and the reconciliation cannot be built until this is settled. A wrong guess means rework.
- **Recommended answer:** Fixed-length 250-character lines exactly as in the attached layout (amounts with 2 implied decimals, dates as YYYYMMDD). Add a total record count on the last line or in a separate file. The mainframe team confirms and sends a sample file.

**Q2. Is this a single load, and how will the file be delivered?** *(PO / Lead)*
- **Story reference:** Title "One time – Prior Data Dump"; Scope "Create a new LNET import job to retrieve Prior Data items from the Mainframe".
- **Question:** Is this one load per environment, or will the mainframe keep sending this file? How will the file reach us, what will it be called, and roughly how many records will it hold?
- **Why we ask:** It decides the job set-up, the schedule and the load time, and whether the regular CHM import must be paused during the load.
- **Recommended answer:** One load per environment, started manually (the job is created switched off). It is delivered the same way as the CHM file, in its own folder with its own file name. The mainframe team gives the file name and expected record count. Loading the same file again creates no duplicates.

**Q3. Is any report expected for this import?** *(PO)*
- **Story reference:** Synopsis "…SSRS reporting structure currently used by the CHM import process"; Scope lists only "Logging, error handling, and reconciliation"; Out of Scope "Downstream workflows after import process".
- **Question:** The synopsis mentions the CHM reporting structure, but no report is listed in scope. Do you expect a new report or a change to the existing CHM customer report?
- **Why we ask:** A report is extra work. Changing the CHM customer report touches a downstream process that is out of scope.
- **Recommended answer:** No new report and no change to the CHM customer report. We provide an import summary (records read, loaded, rejected) and an error email when a load fails.

**Q4. Should this be built with the same tool as the CHM import?** *(Lead)*
- **Story reference:** Scope "Create a new LNET import job" and "import rules similar to CHM import process".
- **Question:** Do we use the same tool as the CHM import (SSIS), or the newer data-pipeline tool (ADF) that also exists on the server?
- **Why we ask:** A different tool means a different build, deployment and support model.
- **Recommended answer:** SSIS, the same as the CHM import, unless the Lead has already decided new imports move to ADF.

**Q5. Who can provide a sample file for testing?** *(Lead + Mainframe team)*
- **Story reference:** AC1 "File is imported using the layout"; also needed to test US-138027 and US-138028.
- **Question:** No sample prior-data file exists. Can the mainframe team provide a small one (about 50–100 records), ideally for parcels that match open CHM records in the test environment?
- **Why we ask:** Without it we cannot confirm the layout, the linking or the screen.
- **Recommended answer:** The mainframe team provides the sample. If it cannot, we build a test file from existing test CHM records and QA runs the load in the test environment.

