## US-138027: Prior Data Store and Linkage

**Q1. Which ID links a prior record to a CHM record?** *(PO + Mainframe team)*
- **Story reference:** Scope "The system should link priors only once for a given tax ID/agency ID" (Agency ID, Tax ID); AC6 "matching prior data record exists".
- **Question:** The file identifies a parcel only by Agency ID and Tax ID. It has no loan number or lender. Loan Details shows "LERETA Tax ID", "Client Tax ID" and an editable "Override TaxID". Which one should match the file's Tax ID?
- **Why we ask:** The wrong ID means priors do not attach, or attach to the wrong record.
- **Recommended answer:** Match Agency ID + LERETA Tax ID as received from the mainframe (not the Override TaxID), ignoring upper/lower case and extra spaces. We verify this against the sample file.

**Q2. When several CHM records share the same Agency ID and Tax ID, which one gets the priors?** *(PO)*
- **Story reference:** Scope "link priors only once for a given tax ID/agency ID"; AC8 "A single CHM record can be associated with multiple prior data records"; AC9 "does not create duplicate prior data records".
- **Question:** The same Agency ID and Tax ID often has several CHM records over time (same loan, different tax year or installment). With "link only once", which record gets the priors? Do they stay there after that record is completed?
- **Why we ask:** It decides which Loan Details screens show prior data. A later CHM record for the same parcel would show none.
- **Recommended answer:** The priors attach to the first Open CHM record found for that Agency ID and Tax ID. They stay on it even after it is completed and are never attached to another record.

**Q3. What does "Open" mean, and when do existing records pick up priors?** *(PO)*
- **Story reference:** Scope and AC7 "When an existing CHM record status is 'Open'… check for any priors… link them"; AC6.
- **Question:** Does "Open" mean only records with the status "O – Open", or every record not yet completed (also New, Worked, Follow-up, Research, Pending QC)? Should they pick up priors right after the prior file is loaded, or only the next time a CHM file is imported?
- **Why we ask:** CHM records created before the one-time load would otherwise show no priors until a later CHM file touches them.
- **Recommended answer:** Open = any CHM record not yet completed. Link them right after the prior load and again on every CHM import.

**Q4. Which story owns the CHM import change?** *(PO / Lead)*
- **Story reference:** US-138027 AC6, AC7; US-138028 Scope "Update the CHM import process to identify and link matching prior data records".
- **Question:** The same change (the CHM import linking priors) is written in both stories. Which story owns it?
- **Why we ask:** To avoid double work or a gap in testing and release.
- **Recommended answer:** US-138027 owns storing and linking, including the CHM import change. US-138028 only shows what is already linked.

