## US-138028: TDT OI UI – Linked CHM Records to Prior Data

*Already decided: prior data is shown in the existing "Prior Information" panel on Loan Details (AC1, AC6).*

**Q1. Should users only view the imported prior data, or also edit it?** *(PO)*
- **Story reference:** Scope "Display prior data as historical information"; AC3; US-138027 AC3 ("without modifying or overwriting the source values") and AC4 ("not merged into the CHM record structure").
- **Question:** Saving in the Prior Information panel copies what is on screen into the loan's own prior information. That information also feeds the CHM customer report, the payment file and transmittal amounts. Should the imported data be view-only?
- **Why we ask:** If users can edit and save it, the imported data flows into those processes (out of scope) and changes their results.
- **Recommended answer:** View-only. Add a clearly labelled read-only block inside the Prior Information panel, with the existing Save and Cancel behaviour unchanged.

**Q2. Which file fields should appear on screen?** *(PO)*
- **Story reference:** AC6 "displays all configured prior data fields according to the approved UI design"; AC4 "Multiple prior data records".
- **Question:** The panel shows Tax Year, Pay Code (PC), Installment 1–4 and Penalty/Interest (P/I) 1–4. It also has one set of two Redeem Amount / Good Thru pairs for the whole loan. The file has the Redeem/Good Thru pairs on every tax-year row. It also has fields the panel has no place for: Bill Type, Penalty-Interest total, Sales Number, and added/updated by and date. Which should be shown?
- **Why we ask:** No separate design was provided, so the field list needs confirming.
- **Recommended answer:** One row per prior tax year, with Tax Year, PC, Installment 1–4, P/I 1–4 and that row's two Redeem Amount / Good Thru pairs. The other file fields are stored but not shown.

**Q3. Is it acceptable that prior data sits behind the existing button and is hidden on the Completed list?** *(PO)*
- **Story reference:** AC2 "When prior data exists… displays the associated historical records"; AC7 "When no prior data is available… not populated".
- **Question:** Today the Prior Information panel stays closed until the user clicks Add Prior / View Prior. It is hidden when a loan is opened from the Completed items list. Is that acceptable for viewing prior data?
- **Why we ask:** Users may not notice the data, and prior data would not be visible on the Completed list.
- **Recommended answer:** Keep it as today: open it with the existing button, with no change to the Completed list. When no priors are linked, the panel looks exactly as it does now.

