## We will proceed with these unless you tell us otherwise
1. All records in the file are loaded, not only those marked HM, and values are kept exactly as received (US-138026 AC1; US-138027 AC3).
2. Records with the same Agency ID, Tax ID, Tax Year and Bill Type count as the same record. A duplicate is skipped and logged, so loading a file twice creates no duplicates (US-138027 AC9).
3. A bad record does not stop the file. It is skipped and logged with its line number, the original line and a clear reason. The load stops only if the file cannot be read. Failure emails go to the same recipients as the CHM import (US-138026 AC2).
4. Prior records with no matching CHM record are kept as they are (US-138027 AC2).
5. A problem while linking never stops the CHM import. It is logged for follow-up.
6. If a tax year exists both as imported and as entered by a user, both are shown and the imported one is labelled (US-138028 AC4, AC5).
7. Prior data appears only on CHM loans, newest tax year first, under the same access rules as Loan Details (US-138028 AC1).
8. No change to the CHM customer report, payment file, transmittal amounts, or the existing Prior Information Save and Cancel.

